# `--explore` gives every run the same standard input, but no longer reads it
# to its end first: with an input held open (a supervisor's pipe; here a FIFO
# the shell holds open for writing) and a program that never reads it, the
# runs go ahead (they waited for ever, until cbtest's wall-clock limit).
platform unix
file p.cb
import std;

fn main()
{
    printf("x\n");
}
end
run sh -c "mkfifo in.fifo && exec 3<>in.fifo && exec $COBC --explore 3 p.cb < in.fifo"
status 0
stdout-starts explored 3 schedules of p.cb: 1 distinct outcome
